; Comparing an account total with an amount compares each of its
; components with the amount, and a component in another commodity makes
; the comparison an error.  Neither a plain number nor a component that
; netted to zero counts as one.
;
; A plain number has no commodity, and compares with an amount by
; quantity, as an amount without a commodity always has.  Assets holds
; $100.00 and 500 points written as a plain number: `total < $200` is
; false for Assets (500 is not below 200) and for Assets:Points, and true
; for Assets:Cash; `total >= $50` holds at both postings of the register.
;
; A component that netted to zero in another commodity is left out of a
; comparison with an amount.  Wallet received 10 EUR and spent them, so
; it prints only $5.00, and it compares as $5.00 does: `total < $10`
; holds and `total < $3` does not, while Tips, which holds $1.00, is
; below $3; Card, at $-10.00 after the same euros, is below $-5.  Ledger
; used to compare the zero EUR with the amount as well, and failed with
; "Cannot compare amounts with different commodities: 'EUR' and '$'":
; always for `total < $10` and `total < $-5`, and for `total < $3`
; whenever it met the EUR before the $5.00 that settles the answer, as
; 3.4.1 did here.  (Against a plain number every component takes part,
; a netted zero included, as it always has.)

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash     $100.00
    Equity

2024/01/02 Loyalty points
    Assets:Points   500
    Income:Points

2024/01/03 Pocket money
    Wallet          $5.00
    Equity

2024/01/04 Euros from a friend
    Wallet          10 EUR
    Income:Gifts

2024/01/05 Dinner
    Expenses:Food   10 EUR
    Wallet

2024/01/06 Tip
    Tips            $1.00
    Equity

2024/01/07 Card payment
    Card            $-10.00
    Equity

2024/01/08 Euros on the card
    Card            10 EUR
    Income:Gifts

2024/01/09 Dinner on the card
    Expenses:Food   10 EUR
    Card

test bal Assets -d 'total < $200'
             $100.00  Assets:Cash
end test

test reg Assets -d 'total >= $50'
24-Jan-01 Opening               Assets:Cash                 $100.00      $100.00
24-Jan-02 Loyalty points        Assets:Points                   500          500
                                                                         $100.00
end test

test bal Wallet -d 'total < $10'
               $5.00  Wallet
end test

test bal Wallet Tips -d 'total < $3'
               $1.00  Tips
end test

test bal Card -d 'total < $-5'
             $-10.00  Card
end test
